+ {"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-23", "title": "[dogfood:P1] extractSection cuts a solution body at its first embedded '---' — any corpus answer containing a horizontal rule swallows everything a community editor appends, and import then reports 'skipped: identical content' (silent no-op where an update is expected)", "priority": "P1", "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-09-25", "labels": ["dogfood", "export-import"], "notes": "internal/import/git.go:561-577 extractSection(content, '## Solution') returns everything up to the FIRST of \\n---\\n, \\n## , \\n# — but formatSolutionMD (internal/export/git.go:432) writes the stored solution TEXT verbatim, and corpus answers commonly END with a '---' rule inside the body (e.g. producer answer id=2 ends '...coercion (e.g., `\"toString\"` as a key).\\n\\n---'). Byte-proven 2026-09-25: appending 'Update v2' text below that rule yields a parsed solution of exactly the old 830 bytes (simulate-parse + sqlite length comparison), so importAnswer's content-diff sees no change and reports ActionSkipped 'identical content' — the community edit silently vanishes at parse time, before conflict logic could ever fire. Fix direction: cut at the LAST marker, or use a unique sentinel (e.g. a final '<!-- off-by-one:solution-end -->' comment the formatter writes), or parse into a markdown AST. Companion fix: when parsed == stored but the raw FILE bytes differ from the last exported/known bytes, report a parse_warning instead of skipped."}
